# 📘 TWO POINTER — COMPLETE NOTES

## 1. What is Two Pointer?

**Two Pointer** ek problem-solving technique hai jisme hum array/string ke **2 indexes (pointers)** ko use karke problem solve karte hain.

Normal approach me hum bahut saare elements ko repeatedly check kar sakte hain.

Two Pointer me hum:

```text
2 pointers
    ↓
intelligently move
    ↓
unnecessary comparisons reduce
    ↓
faster solution
```

### Basic idea

```text
Array:

[ 10  20  30  40  50 ]
   ↑                 ↑
 left              right
```

Yahan:

```cpp
left = 0;
right = n - 1;
```

---

# 2. Why do we use Two Pointer?

Main purpose:

> **Array/string ko efficiently process karna aur unnecessary comparisons ko avoid karna.**

Example:

Brute Force:

```text
har element ko har element ke saath compare
```

Time:

```text
O(n²)
```

Two Pointer:

```text
left/right ko controlled way me move
```

Often:

```text
O(n)
```

ho sakta hai.

⚠️ Lekin **har Two Pointer problem O(n)** nahi hoti. Agar sorting pehle karni pade, total complexity `O(n log n)` bhi ho sakti hai.

---

# 3. Two Pointer ke Main Methods

Two Pointer ko mainly in methods me samjho:

```text
1. Opposite Direction
2. Same Direction
3. Slow & Fast Pointer
4. Sorted Array Pair Method
5. Partition / Rearrangement Method
```

Ab ek-ek ko samjho.

---

# METHOD 1️⃣ — Opposite Direction

## Concept

Ek pointer array ke **start** se aur doosra **end** se start hota hai.

```text
[ 10  20  30  40  50 ]
   ↑                 ↑
 left              right
```

Initialization:

```cpp
int left = 0;
int right = n - 1;
```

Pointers generally center ki taraf move karte hain.

```text
left  → → →
← ← ←  right
```

---

## Kab use kare?

Jab question me:

* first aur last compare karna ho
* array reverse karna ho
* palindrome check karna ho
* pair find karna ho
* two ends ke elements ka relation ho

### Common problems

```text
Reverse Array
Palindrome
Pair Sum
Container With Most Water
3Sum
4Sum
```

---

## General structure

```cpp
while(left < right) {

    // condition check

    left++;
    right--;
}
```

⚠️ Ye exact movement har problem me same nahi hoti. Condition ke according decide karna hota hai.

---

# METHOD 2️⃣ — Pair Sum on Sorted Array

Ye **Two Pointer ka sabse important method** hai.

Suppose sorted array hai:

```text
[ 1  3  5  7  9 ]
  ↑             ↑
 left          right
```

We consider:

```text
currentSum = arr[left] + arr[right]
```

Ab 3 cases.

---

## Case 1: Sum < Target

```text
sum < target
```

Hume sum **increase** karna hai.

Sorted array me left side smaller values hain.

Isliye:

```text
left++
```

### Reason

```text
smaller → bigger
```

Left ko aage le jaoge toh value increase hogi.

---

## Case 2: Sum > Target

```text
sum > target
```

Hume sum **decrease** karna hai.

Right side se value chhoti karni hogi.

```text
right--
```

### Reason

```text
bigger → smaller
```

---

## Case 3: Sum == Target

Required condition mil gayi.

```text
answer found
```

### Golden Rule ⭐

```text
SUM < TARGET
      ↓
    left++

SUM > TARGET
      ↓
    right--

SUM == TARGET
      ↓
    Answer
```

---

# METHOD 3️⃣ — Palindrome / Comparison Method

Is method me bhi:

```text
left = 0
right = n - 1
```

Lekin yahan **sum nahi nikalte**.

Hum dono sides ko compare karte hain.

```text
[ 1  2  3  2  1 ]
  ↑             ↑
 left          right
```

Check:

```text
arr[left] == arr[right]
```

Agar equal:

```text
left++
right--
```

Agar unequal:

```text
Not Palindrome
```

---

## Main idea

> **Outer elements compare karo → andar move karo → repeat karo.**

Iska use:

* Palindrome Array
* Palindrome String
* Valid Palindrome
* Reverse comparison

me hota hai.

---

# METHOD 4️⃣ — Same Direction / Slow-Fast

Ab pointers opposite sides se nahi aayenge.

Dono same side se start karenge.

```text
[ 1  2  3  4  5  6 ]
  ↑
 slow
  ↑
 fast
```

Generally:

```cpp
int slow = 0;
int fast = 0;
```

Lekin dono ka **role different** hota hai.

---

## Fast Pointer ka role

`fast` ka kaam:

> **Array ko scan/explore karna.**

So:

```text
fast → checks elements
```

---

## Slow Pointer ka role

`slow` ka kaam:

> **Valid/required elements ki position maintain karna.**

So:

```text
slow → builds/maintains answer
```

### Easy way to remember:

```text
FAST = Explorer 🔍
SLOW = Builder 🏗️
```

---

# METHOD 5️⃣ — Remove Duplicates

Sorted array:

```text
[ 1  1  2  2  3 ]
```

Yahan hume unique elements maintain karne hain.

Use:

```text
slow + fast
```

Concept:

```text
slow → last valid unique element
fast → new elements search karega
```

Initially:

```text
slow
 ↓
[1  1  2  2  3]
    ↑
   fast
```

Fast jab duplicate dekhe:

```text
same → slow ko move nahi karna
```

Fast jab new value dekhe:

```text
different
    ↓
slow++
    ↓
new value place
```

### Main concept:

```text
FAST → scan
SLOW → valid elements maintain
```

---

# METHOD 6️⃣ — Remove Element

Suppose kuch elements ko remove karna hai.

Hum actually array se physically delete nahi karte.

Instead:

```text
slow → next valid position
fast → scan every element
```

Agar `fast` ko valid element milta hai:

```text
arr[slow] = arr[fast]
slow++
```

Agar unwanted element hai:

```text
slow doesn't move
fast moves
```

### Important idea:

> **Slow pointer answer ka size/position maintain karta hai.**

---

# METHOD 7️⃣ — Move Zeroes / Rearrangement

Suppose:

```text
[0, 1, 0, 3, 12]
```

Goal:

```text
non-zero elements → front
zeroes → end
```

Yahan:

```text
fast → scan
slow → next non-zero position
```

Conceptually:

```text
FAST
 ↓
[0  1  0  3  12]
 ↑
SLOW
```

Fast non-zero element dekhega.

Then slow usko correct position par maintain karega.

### Pattern:

```text
FAST = find useful element
SLOW = place useful element
```

Ye concept bahut important hai.

---

# METHOD 8️⃣ — Partition / Separation

Kabhi question bole:

```text
negative values left
positive values right
```

Ya:

```text
even left
odd right
```

Ya:

```text
0 left
1 right
```

Toh Two Pointer ka partition concept use ho sakta hai.

Pointers:

```text
left → left side
right → right side
```

Concept:

```text
left side ko correct condition maintain karna
right side ko correct condition maintain karna
```

Jab wrong elements milte hain, unko swap/rearrange kar sakte hain.

---

# METHOD 9️⃣ — Container With Most Water Type

Is type me array ke **two ends** se pointers start karte hain.

Conceptually:

```text
[ height values ]

L                    R
↑                    ↑
```

Hum dono boundaries ke beech ka result calculate karte hain.

Important thinking:

> **Kaunsa pointer move karna chahiye?**

Aise questions me movement usually **smaller boundary** ke according decide hoti hai.

Why?

Agar smaller boundary hi limitation hai, toh larger boundary ko move karne se useful height improve nahi hoti; smaller side ko move karke better possibility search karte hain.

### Lesson:

Two Pointer me sirf:

```text
left++
right--
```

important nahi hai.

**Why move?**

Ye sabse important hai.

